        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2023-02-04T22:08:36Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-02-04T22:08:43Z",
        "closed_at": "2023-02-04T22:08:43Z",
        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "draft": false,
        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/react-native-bottom-sheet/pulls/6",
          "merged_at": "2023-02-04T22:08:43Z"
        },
        "body": "when keyboard height updates, an action sheet will animate to a new position\r\n\r\nif this happens on mount, it's possible for values to race in a way where the new position does not match any of the snap points, so `onAnimate` will interpret it as an animation to snap point index -1\r\n\r\nthis normally wouldn't matter since the `fromIndex` is also -1, but as of #3 we get notified of this\r\n\r\none solution here is to pipe through the source of the animation, so callers can check for and ignore anything occurring due to keyboard height changes",
        "reactions": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/react-native-bottom-sheet/issues/6/reactions",
